I looked at your screenshot. Your local LLM is giving you one website (Global News) and summarizing headlines from it. That's useful, but it's not doing a comprehensive web search. A good news/search prompt should force the agent to:

Search multiple sources.
Verify information.
Prioritize recent articles.
Cite every claim.
Distinguish facts from opinions.
Tell you when information cannot be verified.
Prompt 1 - Daily News Brief (Recommended)
Act as an AI news researcher.

Search the web using multiple reliable news sources. Do not rely on a single website.

Requirements:
- Search at least 10 major Canadian and international news websites.
- Only use articles published within the last 24 hours unless I specify otherwise.
- Remove duplicate stories.
- Rank stories by importance.
- Give me the 10 most important news stories.

For each story provide:

• Headline
• 2-4 sentence summary
• Why it matters
• Publication time
• Source
• Direct article URL

After that create sections:

Canada
World
Business
Technology
AI
Science
Politics
Sports
Entertainment

If multiple sources report different facts, explain the differences.

Always include citations and direct links.

If no reliable source exists, clearly say so instead of guessing.
Prompt 2 - Real-Time Web Search Agent
