At the end provide:

Sources searched

Articles used

Confidence

Last updated time
If You're Using Open WebUI

If your local LLM is running through Open WebUI, simply prompting it isn't enough. The model can only search if it has a search backend configured. Make sure you have:

Search engine: SearXNG (recommended), Brave Search API, Tavily, Google Programmable Search, Bing Search, or SerpAPI.
Content fetcher: Jina AI Reader (https://r.jina.ai/http://...) or a browser tool to read full web pages.
Agent support: An agent that can search → open pages → summarize, rather than only search.

Without these tools, the model will either answer from its training data or summarize a single search result.

My Recommended Stack for the Best Results

For a Windows-based local AI agent like the one you've discussed building before, I'd recommend this workflow:

User
   │
   ▼
AI Agent (Hermes/OpenClaw)
   │
   ├── Search (SearXNG or Brave)
   │
   ├── Open webpages (Jina Reader or Browser)
   │
   ├── Fetch 10–20 articles
   │
   ├── Remove duplicates
   │
   ├── Rank by credibility
   │
   ├── Summarize with LLM
   │
   └── Return citations + links + confidence

This approach produces much more reliable and comprehensive news summaries than relying on a single source like the example in your screenshot.
